            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0527" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4704: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-10-22T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 22—9:55
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>398. My 397, October 20, 5 p.m. 1. Following from American consul Canton: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 21, 3 p.m. Your October 20, 5 p.m. Three British and two French
                            river gunboats now in port, also United States ship <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Helena</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pampanga</hi>. United States ship <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Sacramento</hi> at Hongkong. Understand that Russian cruiser <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Vorowsky</hi> still at Whampoa. Japanese consul
                            tells me he will not ask for naval vessel until necessity evident.</p>
                        <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                        <pb facs="0528" n="414" xml:id="pg414"/>
                        <p>Understand that everything essential in customhouse has already been
                            transferred to Shameen and that commissioner could carry on from
                            concession even if Sun seized customs building. Such course might be
                            preferable to forcible measures by the powers.”</p></quote></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
